course: dictionary
lesson: 2061
title: Conservative: one word, many meanings
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word conservative is a good example. «My grandad has conservative taste in music» means he likes traditional music and does not like sudden change. «A conservative estimate» means a careful number, chosen low on purpose so the real figure is probably bigger.
explain: A capital letter can change the meaning. «The Conservative Party» is a real political party in the UK, also called the Tories. A Conservative is a member or supporter of that party. In the USA, the Republican Party is usually called conservative, but it is a different party with its own name.
explain: Context clues tell you which meaning fits. «A conservative suit» is plain and not showy, so the suit has no bright colours or sparkles. Try your meaning in the sentence: if it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Conservative can be an adjective (a conservative suit) or a noun (a conservative is a person who has conservative views).
fact: «Conservative» means not liking sudden change and preferring traditional ways, values and styles.
fact: «A conservative estimate» means a careful guess chosen low on purpose, so the real number is probably bigger.
fact: «The Conservative Party» is one of the main parties in the UK, and it is also called the Tories.
exercise: «My grandad has conservative taste in music.» What does conservative mean here? | Loves every new fashion as soon as it arrives | Plays music very loudly all day | *Likes traditional things and does not like sudden change
exercise: «A conservative estimate of the crowd was 200 people.» What does conservative mean in this sentence? | Counted by a computer | Exactly 200, no more and no less | *Careful and low, so the real number is probably bigger | Very large and generous
exercise: «The Conservative Party» is a political party in the UK. What else is it called? | The Greens | The Republicans | *The Tories | The Liberal Party
test: «He wears a plain, conservative suit to every party.» What does conservative mean? | Bright and shiny | Very old and torn | Covered in sparkly gold buttons | *Plain and not showy
test: «Socially conservative» families usually do what? | *Prefer traditional ways of living and values | Change their customs every week | Have no opinions at all | Eat only in restaurants
exam: «The Labour Party won the 2024 election after 14 years of Conservative governments.» What does Conservative mean here? | A person who is careful with money | *The Conservative Party, a UK political party also called the Tories | A tidy, plain style of clothes | A low guess at a number
